# Dolby DAX (dms) and Dolby Vision (dvs) HAL client memberships restored from stock.
#
# The vendor-CIL de-hack kept only one member of each Dolby client attribute (mtk_hal_audio
# in hal_dms_client, vendorcodec in hal_dvs_client) and dropped every other member. Under
# enforcing this broke Dolby: the client domains could find the HAL hwservice (the de-hack
# kept that allow) but could not binder-call into it, so com.dolby.daxservice (platform_app)
# and com.dolby.dolbyvisionservice (system_app) looped on "unable to call into hwbinder
# service" then aborted, and the audioserver/mediacodec/system_server audio paths would hit
# the same wall on playback.
#
# Restored verbatim from the stock A16 policy (sesearch of the loaded /sys/fs/selinux/policy
# on the TB373FU sibling): hal_dms_client = { audioserver hal_audio_default mediacodec
# mtk_hal_audio platform_app system_server }, hal_dvs_client = { platform_app system_app
# vendorcodec }. Both attributes already carry the find + binder {call transfer} + fd use
# ruleset in mtk_proprietary.te, so joining the attribute is the full grant, identical to
# stock. No app to vendor-HAL neverallow is instantiated for these HALs (the de-hack emitted
# raw allows, not the hal_attribute_hwservice macro).
#
# Placement: this file lives in sepolicy/vendor_mtk_prebuilt (not sepolicy/vendor) on purpose.
# typeattribute requires its attribute already declared, and hal_dms_client/hal_dvs_client are
# declared in mtk_proprietary.te. The build concatenates BOARD_VENDOR_SEPOLICY_DIRS in order
# (sepolicy/vendor first, then sepolicy/vendor_mtk_prebuilt) and sorts .te files within a dir,
# so a file named after "mtk_proprietary.te" here compiles after those declarations. In
# sepolicy/vendor checkpolicy errors with "attribute hal_dms_client is not declared".

# hal_dms_client (mtk_hal_audio already joined in mtk_proprietary.te):
typeattribute audioserver hal_dms_client;
typeattribute hal_audio_default hal_dms_client;
typeattribute mediacodec hal_dms_client;
typeattribute platform_app hal_dms_client;
typeattribute system_server hal_dms_client;

# hal_dvs_client (vendorcodec already joined in mtk_proprietary.te):
typeattribute platform_app hal_dvs_client;
typeattribute system_app hal_dvs_client;

# Dolby DAX AIDL service (vendor.dolby.dms.IDms). A16 exposes Dolby audio over an
# AIDL service alongside the legacy HIDL hal_dms_hwservice. The de-hack left the
# AIDL instance unlabeled (default_android_service), so com.dolby.daxservice
# (platform_app) was denied find under enforcing. Label it and grant find, mirroring
# the Dolby Vision dvs_aidl_service already in service_contexts. hal_dms_default (the
# Dolby DAX HAL) registers it.
type dms_aidl_service;
typeattribute dms_aidl_service service_manager_type;
typeattribute dms_aidl_service hal_service_type;
allow platform_app dms_aidl_service:service_manager find;
allow hal_dms_default dms_aidl_service:service_manager { add find };
